  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces a generalized quantum inner‑product framework for computing weighted sums used in financial engineering and demonstrates small proof‑of‑concept circuits on IBM devices (3–7 qubits, 8192 shots). Hardware experiments measured amplitudes such as ≈0.17747 vs simulated 0.17835 for a discrete‑function expectation and ≈0.72996 vs simulated 0.77998 for a linear‑function expectation. Results validate circuit correctness but are limited to toy instances (N=8) without runtime advantage over classical methods.",
